1
00:00:01,194 --> 00:00:02,308
Hi everyone!

2
00:00:02,374 --> 00:00:08,328
I'll try to shoot a quick tutorial
before the rain gets too heavy.

3
00:00:08,394 --> 00:00:13,490
Today, two fairly simple tricks

4
00:00:13,556 --> 00:00:18,228
you can do once you know how to hop.

5
00:00:18,294 --> 00:00:24,353
They're the "seat drop"

6
00:00:24,419 --> 00:00:29,728
and what's called the "seat bounce".

7
00:00:29,794 --> 00:00:31,240
Let's go!

8
00:00:32,334 --> 00:00:33,615
For this video,

9
00:00:33,681 --> 00:00:37,928
you need to know
how to hop "seat out".

10
00:00:37,994 --> 00:00:41,609
And for these tricks,
you put your feet

11
00:00:41,675 --> 00:00:45,960
on the cranks, because that's easier
than keeping them on the pedals.

12
00:00:47,357 --> 00:00:51,470
So instead of having
your foot...

13
00:00:55,174 --> 00:00:57,840
Instead of having
your foot here on the pedal,

14
00:00:57,928 --> 00:01:01,273
you move it over here,
on the crank.

15
00:01:07,637 --> 00:01:10,150
Let's start with the "seat drop".

16
00:01:13,851 --> 00:01:18,423
What really matters with the "seat drop"
is that once you've moved your foot

17
00:01:18,628 --> 00:01:20,392
from the pedal to the crank,

18
00:01:20,743 --> 00:01:23,956
you put that foot
in the spokes.

19
00:01:24,454 --> 00:01:25,730
So here.

20
00:01:26,134 --> 00:01:30,278
Try to get your toes
to touch the spokes.

21
00:01:30,577 --> 00:01:32,617
I've got a spoke here
that's a bit crooked.

22
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:37,698
What I want to do is use my foot,

23
00:01:37,836 --> 00:01:40,350
my toes, to touch that crooked spoke.

24
00:01:41,544 --> 00:01:47,958
That stops the frame from falling
when you let go of it.

25
00:01:48,144 --> 00:01:50,730
The frame rests
on your toes.

26
00:01:57,987 --> 00:02:02,200
So I hop as usual
with my feet on the cranks.

27
00:02:02,874 --> 00:02:04,860
I tuck my foot in.

28
00:02:06,367 --> 00:02:10,608
I touch the frame.
Now I can let go of the saddle.

29
00:02:10,674 --> 00:02:12,400
And in theory, it shouldn't fall.

30
00:02:22,094 --> 00:02:28,355
You can treat the "seat drop"
as a very simple flatland trick.

31
00:02:28,587 --> 00:02:34,248
And if you practice with friends,
you can set each other challenges.

32
00:02:34,467 --> 00:02:35,816
See who can get the saddle

33
00:02:35,882 --> 00:02:38,869
down to the ground in a "seat drop"
and bring it back up,

34
00:02:38,935 --> 00:02:43,020
or who can last the longest
without holding the saddle.

35
00:02:49,574 --> 00:02:55,664
The second trick to practice
is the "seat bounce".

36
00:02:56,164 --> 00:03:00,748
For this one, you put your feet
on the cranks again.

37
00:03:01,081 --> 00:03:05,488
But this time, you don't put
your toes in the spokes.

38
00:03:05,861 --> 00:03:09,674
The frame mustn't hit your foot
as it comes down.

39
00:03:10,521 --> 00:03:11,894
So nothing should block the frame.

40
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:15,491
It has to be free to drop,
like this, and come back up,

41
00:03:15,744 --> 00:03:17,780
while keeping your foot here.

42
00:03:19,487 --> 00:03:22,954
To start, there are two drills.

43
00:03:23,454 --> 00:03:27,320
How to pick up the saddle
and get low on the unicycle.

44
00:03:28,261 --> 00:03:35,008
Picking up the saddle is pretty much
like in my "drag seat" video.

45
00:03:35,927 --> 00:03:40,460
Try putting one foot on a crank.

46
00:03:41,334 --> 00:03:43,878
To lower the saddle, grab the frame,

47
00:03:44,424 --> 00:03:47,560
and slide your hand along the frame
to set it down.

48
00:03:49,474 --> 00:03:52,620
Grab the bottom of the frame,
then grab it with your other hand.

49
00:03:56,754 --> 00:04:02,665
The second drill is learning
to bend your knees on the unicycle,

50
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:03,887
or learning to get low.

51
00:04:03,954 --> 00:04:07,734
So for this, get on the unicycle,

52
00:04:08,546 --> 00:04:12,067
and try to get your butt
as low as you can.

53
00:04:13,067 --> 00:04:19,160
If you can touch the tire,
that's great.

54
00:04:23,347 --> 00:04:25,840
Next, combine the two drills.

55
00:04:26,227 --> 00:04:29,565
So, to let go of the saddle,

56
00:04:29,824 --> 00:04:35,821
I bend my knees,
slide my hand along the frame,

57
00:04:36,574 --> 00:04:40,284
put the saddle on the ground,
and without letting go of the frame,

58
00:04:40,917 --> 00:04:43,380
I bring the saddle back up
and catch it with my hand.

59
00:04:44,374 --> 00:04:48,777
Always try to keep your back straight

60
00:04:49,176 --> 00:04:55,065
during this exercise,
and keep your center of gravity

61
00:04:55,457 --> 00:04:59,720
over the unicycle's axle,
or you'll fall forward.

62
00:05:14,034 --> 00:05:17,683
When you can tap the saddle
on the ground once,

63
00:05:18,142 --> 00:05:23,980
you can either try setting it down,

64
00:05:24,294 --> 00:05:26,966
coming up, going back down,
and picking it up,

65
00:05:27,439 --> 00:05:30,520
or you can try tapping it
on the ground several times.

